Z||000006||cadaver||09-05-2001||09:43 PM||||So is that a yes or a no to the swap?||||reg||1
Z||000007||GT-maniac||09-05-2001||09:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by cadaver:<BR><B>So is that a yes or a no to the swap?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>From what I've read it's not possible. The later tanks have odd bulges and won't physically fit into the narrower tunnel of the earlier cars. GM apparently redesigned the floorpan to get the larger tank in.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero005a.jpg"> <P>85 WS6 GT partly modified<BR>87 GT Loaded resto project||||reg||1
Z||000008||Jake_Dragon||09-05-2001||10:14 PM||||OK  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> I can never get more than 8 gallons in my 85 and I let it get very low, as in run out. <P>Not really a question I know the answer, looking at where the fuel pump is placed in the tank it cannot pickup the last two gallons.||||reg||1
